WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.374
Host: Explain how ATP can support glucose
uptake without binding to its cotransporter.

2
00:00:06.374 --> 00:00:14.232
Guide: ATP powers the sodium–potassium pump,
which maintains a low intracellular sodium
concentration.

3
00:00:14.232 --> 00:00:19.670
Guide: Sodium then enters through a
cotransporter down its electrochemical
gradient,

4
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.344
Guide: providing energy for coupled glucose
uptake.

5
00:00:23.344 --> 00:00:31.557
Host: The sodium–potassium pump is inhibited
in a teaching model. Why might sodium–glucose
uptake weaken later?

6
00:00:31.557 --> 00:00:39.496
Guide: The sodium gradient gradually becomes
less able to power cotransport. The pump
maintains the gradient;

7
00:00:39.496 --> 00:00:44.884
Guide: its loss eventually reduces the energy
available to secondary transport.
